00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:54.000
real users. Don't just test yourself.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:55.600
Get someone else use your app [music]

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.959
and watch them. How do they interact

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.480
with it? What's their feedback? You'll

00:08:56.959 --> 00:09:00.000
see confusion you never noticed because

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:01.680
everyone interacts with technology

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.720
differently. You'll catch bugs you never

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.399
triggered. Second, [music] you want to

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:06.800
test under real conditions. For example,

00:09:04.399 --> 00:09:08.160
my agent/ app that booked shifts. I test

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:09.920
it when the shift actually drops. For

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:11.519
example, your chatbot handles inquiries.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:13.360
Test it with real customer questions,

00:09:11.519 --> 00:09:14.800
not the sanitized ones you made up where

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.800
you know what the output's going to be.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:18.560
Third, get paid before you finish. This

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:20.800
is my favorite. My shift booking agent

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:22.480
was probably like 70% [music] good. I

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.920
already had clients paying. Why? Because

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.880
it worked. It wasn't perfect, but it

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:25.920
solved their problem, and that's all

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.839
that matters. Now, here's the thing

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:29.220
about AI. It will sound confident even

00:09:27.839 --> 00:09:31.040
when it's wrong. I I honestly hate

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:32.880
[music] this. Makes me so mad. So, make

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:34.480
sure you're careful with it because you

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.240
have to verify every [music] every claim

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:38.160
you make about what your solution can do

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:40.080
or can't do because if you just go by

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.200
with the AI saying, it can literally be

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:42.720
wrong. [music] By the time you finish

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:44.080
week three, you should have at least one

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.000
person who has used a solution and

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:48.080
confirm it works. And now it's time to

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.440
develop your taste. Most people build AI

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.959
businesses like they're using a vending

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:52.800
machine. They push a button, [music]

00:09:50.959 --> 00:09:54.560
grab whatever generic output comes out,

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:56.399
and wonder why nobody's buying. So, how

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:58.160
do you stand out? You develop taste. For

00:09:56.399 --> 00:10:00.399
example, my student Liddon built his a

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.760
dental AI system for a Texas dentist. He

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:03.279
didn't just slap together generic. What

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:05.519
he built was a dashboard with high

00:10:03.279 --> 00:10:07.200
in-depth analytics, call tracking. It

00:10:05.519 --> 00:10:08.640
was fully customade. It integrated

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:10.399
perfectly with the chatbot, stored

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:11.920
leads, handled missed calls, cancel

00:10:10.399 --> 00:10:13.760
appointments, did absolutely everything.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.440
And the questions he asked was what

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:17.017
would make the dentist's jaw drop and

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:18.480
what would make him tell other dentists

00:10:17.017 --> 00:10:19.760
[music] about it. And that's how he was

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:22.079
able to land that client. And of course,

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:23.760
he had a great mentor. And then me and

00:10:22.079 --> 00:10:25.440
him pitched the idea together where we

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:27.360
would tell that dentist that we will

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:29.040
give him a finder fee if he is able to

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.880
bring some of his friends on board on

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:32.320
the solution. That's taste. Building

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:34.000
something that makes people want to

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:36.320
share it. Here's a framework I use and

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:37.920
teach. Stand. S is for specific. Is the

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:39.300
solution laser focused on one problem?

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:41.120
If not, narrow it. T is for tangible.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:43.279
[music] Can you show measurable results,

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.720
screenshots, metrics, testimonials? A is

00:10:43.279 --> 00:10:46.399
for automated. Does the solution

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:48.000
actually save time or effort? If it

00:10:46.399 --> 00:10:49.600
requires manual work from the client,

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.077
it's not really valuable enough. N is

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.720
for new. Does it feel fresh or does

00:10:51.077 --> 00:10:54.399
[music] she like every other AI tool out

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:56.240
there like voice AI receptionist for

00:10:54.399 --> 00:10:57.600
dentists? I thought everyone wants to do

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:59.760
that nowadays. And because the industry

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:01.279
is so far behind, it still works, but it

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.640
will become saturated at a point. And D

00:11:01.279 --> 00:11:03.680
is for delightful. Is there something

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.839
about your solution that makes [music]

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:08.000
people smile, a small touch that shows

00:11:05.839 --> 00:11:09.600
you care? As you apply this over 30

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:11.360
days, you start noticing something

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:13.040
deeper. Every problem you solve, every

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:14.480
client you talk to, every iteration you

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:15.279
make, you're not just building a

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.120
business. [music] You're training

00:11:15.279 --> 00:11:19.440
yourself to see the world differently.

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:21.200
The eyes of automation. Most people are

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:22.880
paralyzed by the AI revolution. They see

